WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.730
In Westworld Season 2 Episode 4, Bernard is
dragged on his arse by Clementine, who grabbed

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.360
him last episode.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.680
She drags him to a cave that’s “miles”
from anywhere , which means A) Bernard’s

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.809
butt must hurt, and B)

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:14.500
there’s a secret here.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.730
Inside, Bernard finds Elsie – last season,
Ford programmed Bernard to capture her, cause

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.910
she almost found out Ford’s plans.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:27.670
Apparently, Elsie’s survived on protein
bars ever since . Bernard frees Elsie, and

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.289
she finds out Bernard is host.

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:33.650
She takes the news pretty well that that her
boss was a robot along.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:39.070
Her curiosity as a programmer is greater than
her fear – so she helps with Bernard’s

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.070
brain damage.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:45.200
They find a secret Delos lab, like the lab
in Episode 1 where drone hosts record guest

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.649
data . But this lab is something more – it
has James Delos.

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:55.860
About thirty years ago, James died of a disease
. But his company, led by William, copied

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:02.520
his mind into a robot body – a hybrid of
human and host . The goal was to make James

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.520
immortal.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.249
But this human-host is unstable, it breaks
down . So the company keeps burning James

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:12.829
and making a new one, achieving a longer life
each time.

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:17.679
Over thirty years, he is born then dies one
hundred and forty-nine times , having the

00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:21.180
same conversation with William over and over.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.210
The imagery of a spinning record and exercise
bike and circular room evoke the loop that

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.810
James is trapped in.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.459
He finds out that his wife and kids are dead
over and over.

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:36.420
He’s burned alive over and over, to the
soundtrack of the Rolling Stones’ Play With

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.420
Fire.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.840
He had tried to “cheat the devil” and
live forever, but he ended up in hell.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.789
By the time of Season 1, William’s wife
Juliet has died, and he’s stopped believing

00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:51.880
in the immortality project – saying “People
aren't meant to live forever” . So he leaves

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:57.079
James to break down, and then the robot revolution
happens so there’s no one to terminate James

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:00.460
until Bernard and Elsie find him two weeks
later.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:06.240
By then, James is mad and suffering, which
may be the closest he’s been to alive.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.860
Cause one of the big ideas last season is
that suffering makes hosts conscious and free

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:18.890
. So maybe in Jim’s pain and death, he felt
alive for the first time in decades.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:24.200
So this is part of the Delos secret project
that’s been hinted at all series . They’re

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.150
trying to make humans immortal by putting
their minds in host bodies.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:32.739
But how does this connect to the Westworld
guest behaviour data recorded in these labs

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:35.239
? And whose brains are these?

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:40.019
To clone James, he has an “observation period”
and “baseline interview” – they make

00:02:40.019 --> 00:02:45.410
a record of who James is so they can copy
him with high “fidelity” . Westworld is

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.329
kinda the same thing.

00:02:47.329 --> 00:02:53.019
William says the park reveals who guests really
are , through their choices and sins – and

00:02:53.019 --> 00:02:55.310
Delos has been watching.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:00.530
With this “baseline” data , maybe Delos
can make human-host clones of all Westworld

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:01.530
guests.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:06.069
And as we see with Jim’s script, these hybrid
hosts are predictable.

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:12.819
Maybe Delos could use this technology to control
human behaviour . This could be Glory – Dolores’

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:18.430
weapon , William’s mistake , the burning
of the species Logan mentions – not human-like

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:24.349
robots, but robot-like humans . We don’t
know the details, but Glory must be something

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:29.530
that combines humanity and hosts, immortality
and control.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.840
And there’s another mystery here.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.390
We find out that sometime round Season 1,
Ford sent Bernard to this lab to kill the

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:40.620
techs and make another hybrid brain of some
human.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.659
Whose mind did they build?

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:45.980
One possibility is Ford – maybe they’ll
bring him back.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:51.719
But Ford’s death made a point about the
end of the humans and rise of the hosts . Ford

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:57.130
said he’ll live on in his music – he exists
in the code of his hosts like Lawrence’s

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.959
daughter and young Robert.

00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:04.209
So bringing back Ford as a hybrid-host would
undermine the climax of last season.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:08.810
Maybe this host could be a young William to
confront old Bill at the end of his quest

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:15.349
– he is told to revisit his past . Or maybe
this mind will be Arnold’s – Ford’s

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:17.509
partner who Bernard is based on.

00:04:17.509 --> 00:04:21.739
If they wanna get tricky, it could be that
the Bernard we saw in the week ahead timeline

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:28.140
in Episode 1 is actually Arnold as a human-host
hybrid . Because he’s acting super weird,

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.130
and he has flashbacks of Arnold with Dolores.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:34.270
How could Bernard remember Arnold’s life?

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:38.990
Last season, Westworld showed us Arnold and
made us think it was Bernard – maybe they’re

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:41.450
pulling the same trick this season.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:44.180
So this hybrid mind might be Arnold’s.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:49.620
But there is one more complication – what’s
the data in Peter Abernathy’s head.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.150
Is it a copy of James Delos’ mind?

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.669
Or Arnold’s mind?

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:57.560
Charlotte said there’s “Thirty-five years
of … data” in there , so maybe it’s

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:03.470
all the guest behaviour and DNA data – that
might explain why Delos needs it so bad.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:08.560
William and Lawrence see Chinese railway worker
hosts who kill their overseers and use their

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.819
bodies as railroad ties.

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:16.830
Chinese railway workers in the real American
west suffered dangerous conditions and discrimination.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:21.850
So along with colonial India, and Confederate
slavery, Westworld explores real historical

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:25.419
injustice to parallel the treatment of hosts.

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:29.910
It also looks at violent revenge, personified
by Dolores.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:35.190
Is it justice to kill your masters, or, as
Maeve suggests, does revenge just make you

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:40.879
just as bad as them ? Bill and Lawrence arrive
as Las Mudas, the home of Lawrence’s wife

00:05:40.879 --> 00:05:41.879
and daughter.

00:05:41.879 --> 00:05:46.509
Lawrence says that his family loves him, but
really he’s “a son of a bitch”, so it’s

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:51.250
kinder for him to avoid his family . This
is similar to William’s situation – he

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:55.610
had a wife and daughter , but he’s a bad
dude, and spent time in Westworld instead

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:59.139
of with them .
The town is controlled by Craddock.

00:05:59.139 --> 00:06:04.050
He holds court in a church and brags about
his resurrection earlier – says he’s the

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:09.990
chosen one of death . This annoys William,
because he believes death is final, and people

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:15.189
shouldn’t be brought back . And then Craddock
starts murdering and tormenting the townspeople

00:06:15.189 --> 00:06:18.900
– just like William did when he was here
last season.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:24.750
So Bill is faced with his own past sins, and
this time, he feels some sympathy for the

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.750
hosts.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:29.660
Lawrence’s wife reminds him of the death
of his own wife, Juliet.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:35.069
So the Man in Black takes on the role of death,
and kills Craddock and his men in the rain.

00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:41.780
Showrunner Lisa Joy says this represents washing
away Bill’s past – trying to achieve redemption

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:47.009
. Lawrence’s family thank him for the help
, but Lawrence’s daughter, speaking as Ford,

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:52.689
says one good deed doesn’t erase William’s
crimes . So this season, we’re getting a

00:06:52.689 --> 00:06:54.970
more morally ambiguous William.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:59.129
Last season, he was a villain, but now he’s
trying to make things right.

00:06:59.129 --> 00:07:02.639
As Lawrence’s daughter says, “If you're
looking forward, you're looking in the wrong

00:07:02.639 --> 00:07:06.599
direction” – William is facing his past.

00:07:06.599 --> 00:07:09.850
We see Grace, the woman from The Raj last
episode.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:14.840
She’s been captured by Ghost Nation, along
with some guests from Season 1 – tourists

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.910
who get more than they bargained for.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.680
There’s also Stubbs, captured last season.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:24.460
He says that while Ghost Nation does kill
hosts, they don’t kill humans.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:29.199
Ghost Nation takes their prisoners to Akecheta,
who they call “the first of us” . Maybe

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:34.909
Akecheta was first Ghost Nation host created
– we do see him as an early host in Episode

00:07:34.909 --> 00:07:35.909
2.

00:07:35.909 --> 00:07:41.061
Grace escapes, then Akecheta threatens Stubbs,
and says “You live only as long as the last

00:07:41.061 --> 00:07:45.949
person who remembers you” , which connects
to the themes of legacy and immortality with

00:07:45.949 --> 00:07:47.240
James.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:52.210
Then the Ghost Nation hosts disappear – apparently
letting Stubbs leave and meet up with Delos

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.250
for the week ahead timeline.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.659
Why would Ghost Nation capture humans then
let them go?

00:07:57.659 --> 00:07:59.889
Are these hosts programmed, or free?

00:07:59.889 --> 00:08:02.569
Are they protecting humans, or doing something
else?

00:08:02.569 --> 00:08:04.610
We still don’t know.

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:09.750
In the end, Grace meets William, and reveals
that she is his daughter, Emily – maybe

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.699
Grace is a fake name.

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:16.340
We know from last season that Emily and William
have a difficult relationship.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:21.439
She blames Bill for the suicide of her mother
Juliet , and Bill says his daughter would

00:08:21.439 --> 00:08:26.510
“Probably” like to see him gunned down
. So this isn’t the happiest reunion.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:32.230
But Bill and Emily seem to have the same goal
– to reach Glory, symbolised by this hexagonal

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:34.890
pattern that appears in Delos labs.

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:39.470
Now that we know about James’ immortality
project, this symbol almost looks like an

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:43.300
infinity sign, or an hourglass tipped on its
side.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:48.220
William and Grace might need to work together
to reach the mystery at the centre of this

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:49.400
season.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.960
Thank you for watching.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:56.120
And thanks to the Patrons, including MELINDA
RUBIN, Matthew Athey, isrightkev, Gareth Foot,

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.240
and hayburtz.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.040
Cheers.

